    <div class="prose">
      <p class="lead"><strong>Three specs decide it: weight, shaft flex and balance.</strong> For a club player that means 4U or 5U, a medium or flexible shaft, and even balance, and you can buy all of it for £30 to £80. Above about £80 the market starts selling you a professional's racket instead: heavier in the head, stiffer in the shaft, and increasingly with no strings in the box.</p>

      <p>Get it wrong and you will spend £150 finding out that the racket was never the thing holding you back.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="guide-callout" style="margin-top:30px">
      <h4>The short version</h4>
      <ul style="margin:10px 0 0">
        <li><strong>Buy 4U or 5U, medium or flexible shaft, even balance.</strong> That is the whole club specification, and the cheapest racket we found carrying all of it was £24.95.</li>
        <li><strong>£30 to £80 is the band.</strong> Above roughly £80 the specs do not stop improving, they start pointing at somebody else.</li>
        <li><strong>Check whether it comes strung.</strong> Above £120 most rackets do not, and a restring is another £12 to £25.</li>
        <li><strong>Head-heavy will not make your smash faster.</strong> That is measured, not opinion.</li>
        <li><strong>The racket is not your limiting factor.</strong> Where you hit the shuttle and how fast you swing account for most of it.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <p style="margin-top:22px;color:var(--muted-2);font-size:.95rem">Written for adults buying a first or second badminton racket in the UK, playing club or social badminton. Market figures come from our own count of 228 adult rackets in Badminton HQ's catalogue on 23 August 2026, with the trends checked against Central Sports. Specifications are the retailers' own product tags describing how each racket is marketed, not measurements we took. <strong>We have no commercial relationship with any racket manufacturer or retailer, and nothing on this page earns us anything.</strong> The full method is at the foot of this guide.</p>

    <div class="guide-toc" style="margin-top:26px">
      <h4>In this guide</h4>
      <a href="#which-specs">Which specs actually decide it?</a>
      <a href="#laws">What do the Laws require?</a>
      <a href="#weight">Weight: what do 3U, 4U and 5U mean?</a>
      <a href="#balance">Does a head-heavy racket make you hit harder?</a>
      <a href="#flex">Shaft flex: stiff or flexible?</a>
      <a href="#grip">Grip size: does it matter?</a>
      <a href="#strung">Does it come strung?</a>
      <a href="#spend">How much should you spend?</a>
      <a href="#cheap">What does the cheap shelf actually sell you?</a>
      <a href="#ignore">What should you ignore?</a>
      <a href="#demo">Can you try before you buy?</a>
